            "nearby": "Volunteering in Pacifica Over the past 20+ years, I’ve always been driven to serve my local community in some fashion. I joined the Pacifica Mothers Club (now the Pacifica Families Club) even before arriving in town, and I held various positions with that wonderful organization, including President. I’ve been deeply involved with the Pacific Beach Coalition since 2005, serving on the Board, as a standby site captain, and more recently on the Communications Team. I fully believe in PBC’s mission of environmental conservation and education. When my kids attended Ortega Elementary and then IBL Middle School, I was active in the PTOs and spent many years leading beautification efforts at Ortega. Since moving to Pacifica, I also have become a climate activist as I witness our planet’s health being compromised by fossil fuel emissions. I trained as a Climate Reality leader in 2021 and have joined a number of climate efforts, including the recent citizen task force that put together the City of Pacifica’s current climate action plan. Currently, I am Vice Chair of the Climate Action and Resilience Committee, which is tasked with implementing the climate action plan.",
